# dev-notes.28 — worker-layout-option-c-router-v1

Date: 2026-06-07
Branch/slice: worker-layout-option-c-router-v1

## Purpose

Extract the worker-side message routing body from `llama_worker/llama.mjs` into `llama_worker/messages/workerProtocolRouter.mjs` while preserving `llama_worker/llama.mjs` as the worker entrypoint and composition root.

## Scope

Added:

```text
llama_worker/messages/workerProtocolRouter.mjs
```

Modified:

```text
llama_worker/llama.mjs
tests/helpers/runtimeFixtureFiles.mjs
fixture-copy smoke tests with local RUNTIME_FILES arrays
```

## Preserved behavior

The router extraction preserves the current worker route behavior:

```text
init: set active init config, init model, return
cancel: bypass lifecycle serialization, build prompt abort metadata, abort active request, return
shutdown: enqueue serialized shutdown, post shutdown_done after completion, return
reset_session: enqueue serialized reset_session, assert ready inside operation, reset session, post reset_done with sessionId, return
reset_model: enqueue serialized reset_model, assert ready inside operation, reset model, post model_reset_done, return
prompt: assert ready before handlePromptMessage(msg)
unknown message: no-op fallthrough
catch/error: preserve initErrorMeta fallback and postWorkerError shape
```

## Non-goals

This branch does not change parent runtime code, worker protocol shapes, lifecycle service behavior, prompt runner cleanup ownership, context/session behavior, config/retry behavior, model path behavior, cancellation semantics, cleanup, or optimization.

## Propagation

`llama_worker/messages/workerProtocolRouter.mjs` was added to the shared runtime fixture list and the active fixture-copy smoke tests that still maintain local `RUNTIME_FILES` arrays.

